    <h1>Oliver!</h1>

    
    
        
        
    <div  class="bard-content">
        <p><em>It’s a Fine Life</em> at the Gielgud Theatre where <strong><em>Oliver!</em></strong>, the award-winning production reconceived by <strong>Cameron Mackintosh</strong> and director and choreographer <strong>Matthew Bourne</strong>, is playing its second triumphant year in the West End.<br><br>The Olivier, Tony and Oscar-winning classic with its sensational score featuring the iconic songs <em>Food Glorious Food</em>, <em>Where is Love?</em>, <em>Oom-Pah-Pah</em>, <em>As Long as He Needs Me</em> and <em>Reviewing the Situation </em>vividly brings to life Dickens’ London and the ever-popular story of the boy who asked for more.<br><br>With a standout cast lead by <strong>Matt Lucas </strong><span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);">as Fagin, for six weeks only</span>, <strong>Ava Brennan</strong> as Nancy, <strong>Aaron Sidwell</strong> as Bill Sikes and <strong>Aaron MacGregor</strong> as the Artful Dodger, <strong>Lionel Bart</strong>’s iconic musical is brought to life by <strong>Lez Brotherston</strong>’s design and Olivier-Award winning lighting from <strong>Paule Constable</strong> and <strong>Ben Jacobs</strong>. <strong>Simon Lipkin </strong><span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);">returns as</span><strong> </strong><span style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);">Fagin from 3 November.</span></p><p>​There’s no need to <em>Pick a Pocket</em> for a ticket: buying direct means access to <a href="#ways-to-save/family-tickets">Family Tickets</a> and the <a href="#ways-to-save/ticket-lotteries">weekly lottery</a> and with no booking fees and exchange up to 48 hours before your performance, the only answer to ‘<em>Who will Buy</em>?’, is you! And, if you can’t wait to <em>Be Back Soon</em>, don’t miss our <a href="#gallery/podcasts">podcast</a> episodes with Lez and Simon talking all things <strong><em>Oliver!</em></strong>.</p><p>So, <em>Consider Yourself</em> well in this summer and book your tickets now for the ultimate British musical that generations continue to fall in love with.</p>
    </div>


    
        
        







    
    




    








    
    
    




    



